The class `CompletableFromUnsafeSource` is a thin delegating wrapper that simply forwards the subscription to an underlying `CompletableSource`. It contains no computational logic, state changes, or algorithmic complexity that would benefit from micro‑benchmarking. Measuring its performance with JMH would primarily capture the overhead of the RxJava subscription mechanism itself, which is already well‑covered by existing RxJava benchmarks and is not specific to this class. Therefore, generating a dedicated JMH benchmark is unnecessary.